cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "qi-vc-poc: Verifiable Credentials for Quality Infrastructure"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-05-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/monavari/VC4QI
abstract: >
  A polyglot (TypeScript + Python) reference implementation of W3C Verifiable
  Credentials 2.0 for quality infrastructure use cases including calibration
  certificates (DCC) and reference material certificates (DRMD).
  Implements the three-layer credential architecture (AccreditationCredential →
  CapabilityCredential → Domain Credentials) with eddsa-rdfc-2022 Data Integrity
  proofs, URDNA2015 canonicalization, Bitstring Status List v1.0, and a
  scope-bounded verification engine (six deterministic rules). Includes 160
  automated tests (87 TypeScript + 12 scenario + 61 Python) and serves as the
  reference implementation for the paper "A Scope-Bounded Verifiable Credentials
  Architecture for Digital Calibration and Reference Material Certificates"
  (Monavari et al., MDPI Sensors, 2026).
authors:
  - family-names: Monavari
    given-names: Mehran
    email: monavari.mehran@gmail.com
keywords:
  - verifiable-credentials
  - quality-infrastructure
  - calibration
  - accreditation
  - w3c-vc
  - data-integrity
references:
  - type: software
    title: "VC-calibration-chain"
    version: 0.1.0
    authors:
      - family-names: Monavari
        given-names: Mehran
    repository-code: https://github.com/mehranmo/VC-calibration-chain
    notes: >
      Prior art v0.1; qi-vc-poc is the successor implementation. Schemas and
      verification policy architecture derive from this work.
